-- Training room: the typical-wine audit (data only).
--
-- Owner, 2026-09-28: "double check the typical wines. Its very very good right
-- now but i want it to be perfect". All 102 typical wines were audited field by
-- field against WSET materials, the Oxford Companion, Jancis Robinson,
-- appellation rules and regional bodies (14 regional batches plus three
-- cross-set passes: structure, aroma groups and signatures, and grapes,
-- designations, ages and places). Every proposed change was voted on by three
-- independent checks (examiner, source-checker, effect on the ranking); this
-- migration carries the changes a majority accepted, plus the owner-list items
-- the synthesis recommended. Not here: anything that waits on the aroma
-- lexicon changes (apple split, dried/cooked fruit leaving the primary list,
-- smoked meat and olive), which ship with the lexicon migration; the
-- Pessac-Léognan designation (its label says "Cru Classé de Graves", which is
-- no type_designations row yet); and years-from-vintage age hints on
-- non-vintage sparkling wines (Champagne, Cava, Franciacorta), left null like
-- Fino and Manzanilla. Every change with its sources and votes:
-- data/training/archetype-audit-2026-09-28.json.
--
-- Written against the live state of 2026-09-28: every value changed here is
-- asserted to be what the audit read before anything is written, and asserted
-- again afterwards. The pool is read per request, so the room reflects it at
-- once. No begin/commit: the applier owns the transaction.

